[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186124542 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-15721919-affc-527a-806f-d54311da77ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-15721919-affc-527a-806f-d54311da77ac" :question/id #uuid "15721919-affc-527a-806f-d54311da77ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-97580" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-daee834d-972a-5370-8934-102b16e2168b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-daee834d-972a-5370-8934-102b16e2168b" :answer-field/id #uuid "daee834d-972a-5370-8934-102b16e2168b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-209da59d-2b86-550d-89c6-5385f915b5e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15d13c75-e6bc-5e2e-a8a5-6dd560e659ae" "answer-d70dba8c-62c5-5199-93bd-0c9dd94ff141" "answer-bfe4a7d2-be73-53f9-b806-31ea43cf2ba9" "answer-209da59d-2b86-550d-89c6-5385f915b5e2" "answer-570944f0-ed2d-54ac-afa7-c23ef2d1f070"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15d13c75-e6bc-5e2e-a8a5-6dd560e659ae" :answer/id #uuid "15d13c75-e6bc-5e2e-a8a5-6dd560e659ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d70dba8c-62c5-5199-93bd-0c9dd94ff141" :answer/id #uuid "d70dba8c-62c5-5199-93bd-0c9dd94ff141" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfe4a7d2-be73-53f9-b806-31ea43cf2ba9" :answer/id #uuid "bfe4a7d2-be73-53f9-b806-31ea43cf2ba9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-209da59d-2b86-550d-89c6-5385f915b5e2" :answer/id #uuid "209da59d-2b86-550d-89c6-5385f915b5e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-570944f0-ed2d-54ac-afa7-c23ef2d1f070" :answer/id #uuid "570944f0-ed2d-54ac-afa7-c23ef2d1f070" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119844 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fc096f25-da43-5ef0-8dca-9310fea097c1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fc096f25-da43-5ef0-8dca-9310fea097c1" :question/id #uuid "fc096f25-da43-5ef0-8dca-9310fea097c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42981" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+8y=-28 \\\\ 2x+3y=11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{x}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+8y=-28 \\\\ 2x+3y=11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\,-28 & 8 \\\\ \\,\\,11 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8429c5f3-10e5-5e89-82ae-2a624d986bbe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8429c5f3-10e5-5e89-82ae-2a624d986bbe" :answer-field/id #uuid "8429c5f3-10e5-5e89-82ae-2a624d986bbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-752e27ae-6bc8-5acc-bb2a-b47134fc80d9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8a477f06-b877-5fa0-bce3-9f5744ae6971" "answer-41433e06-ff80-564d-9ce3-d0dc9852a8ee" "answer-249e501c-2f96-5d3a-aca1-a06ed673e1ac" "answer-752e27ae-6bc8-5acc-bb2a-b47134fc80d9" "answer-2592d63c-e1be-5dbf-bf09-9ff0d9f2f561"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a477f06-b877-5fa0-bce3-9f5744ae6971" :answer/id #uuid "8a477f06-b877-5fa0-bce3-9f5744ae6971" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & \\,-28 \\\\ 2 & \\,11\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41433e06-ff80-564d-9ce3-d0dc9852a8ee" :answer/id #uuid "41433e06-ff80-564d-9ce3-d0dc9852a8ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-249e501c-2f96-5d3a-aca1-a06ed673e1ac" :answer/id #uuid "249e501c-2f96-5d3a-aca1-a06ed673e1ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}\\,-28 & 5 \\\\ \\,\\,11 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-752e27ae-6bc8-5acc-bb2a-b47134fc80d9" :answer/id #uuid "752e27ae-6bc8-5acc-bb2a-b47134fc80d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}\\,-28 & 8 \\\\ \\,\\,11 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2592d63c-e1be-5dbf-bf09-9ff0d9f2f561" :answer/id #uuid "2592d63c-e1be-5dbf-bf09-9ff0d9f2f561" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}\\,11 & 8 \\\\ \\,-28 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192676 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2595de8f-014d-5db6-a5d3-e22363b7564e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2595de8f-014d-5db6-a5d3-e22363b7564e" :question/id #uuid "2595de8f-014d-5db6-a5d3-e22363b7564e" :question/math-academy-id "q-152903" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[9X+4].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x}{2},\\,0<x<2\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[9X+4]=9\\text{E}[X]+4\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[9X+4] & =9\\text{E}[X]+4 \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}+4 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d5917ecc-743e-5b98-928c-b4e265150550"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d5917ecc-743e-5b98-928c-b4e265150550" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5917ecc-743e-5b98-928c-b4e265150550" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a24492a0-f30c-5760-a699-262c2d5c1e9b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-00390579-73db-58de-8e3f-f3ca75d10676" "answer-a24492a0-f30c-5760-a699-262c2d5c1e9b" "answer-76eeaeb4-2ab6-520a-b6b0-9a2f15095f14" "answer-6ca1573d-75dd-57d1-975d-20b4eabf81d0" "answer-b388bc7a-f341-596b-93dd-60183e4ec2b1"] :db/ensure [:answ